From 4f0f77b69a87d90a2944df145b2c9810b480b2fd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Doctor Logix <doctor.logix@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 17:48:01 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 157/162] media: i2c: add the Dongwoon DW9785 lens focus driver

The DW9785 drives the focus and the optical image stabilisation of a
camera module from its own DSP. This driver drives the focus only, as
a lens subdevice with V4L2_CID_FOCUS_ABSOLUTE from 0 to 4095.

Power comes up as the nx809j stock sequence has it: I/O, actuator,
then the stabiliser supply, 4 ms. The start-up list is the stock one:
logic reset (0xd002), DSP on (0xd001), then 0xdd03 and 0xdd04 at 2.
The chip ID (0x7000) reads 0x9785 once the DSP runs. The focus target
is 0x7070.

Checked on the nx809j main camera: frames of a shelf at 3 m and of a
chart at 12 cm each turn sharp at their own target and blur on both
sides. As with dw9719, the lens is powered while its node is open.

(cherry picked from commit 80b98c0260c4a389f51090f7f5900b568df94f54)
